{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"---\nname: turnbridge-mvp-decisions\ndescription: Turnbridge intent decisions (2026-07-19 MVP, 2026-07-21 end-state) and implementation state\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e\n  modified: 2026-07-21T22:35:08.238Z\n---\n\nDecisions made by the user on 2026-07-19 that override the original design docs:\n\n- Turnbridge is the **resume layer only**; conversation-ledger owns capture\n  (its `cledger install` hooks + adapters already existed and are reused).\n- Cross-CLI rehydration **defaults to native session fabrication** (writing\n  target-native session files so the CLI's own resume loads them);\n  `--bootstrap` (transcript-file rehydration) is the explicit fallback.\n- MVP audience: the user hopping CLIs **and** sharing chats with collaborators\n  who use different CLIs — own chats by default, `--all` for others', identity\n  via git `user.email` stamped as `actor.id` (upstream cledger change).\n- Command surface: standalone `turnbridge resume [claude|codex]` is default;\n  the PATH shim (`turnbridge shim install`) is opt-in, may become default\n  later if it proves stable over a few weeks.\n- Picker UX the user described: pick conversation → asked which CLI → offered\n  to save that choice as default.\n\nImplementation state: MVP works end-to-end; fabrication verified against real\nbinaries (claude 2.1.215, codex-cli 0.144.6) via planted-secret resume tests.\nVersion-pinned format specs live in turnbridge `docs/specs/`. Upstream\nconversation-ledger gained `package.json` exports + `gitUserIdentity` actor\nstamping (note: full transcript rescans can duplicate pre-identity events\nsince `actor.id` is part of the event-id hash).\n\nEnd-state decisions from 2026-07-21 (drive TODO priority):\n- **Public npm release** is the goal — the `file:../conversation-ledger` dep\n  must become a p