tion is version-pinned, bootstrap\n116\tis the recovery path); transcript content can include secrets (the ledger\n117\tredacts at capture and sync time, but matching is pattern/entropy-based and\n118\tcannot catch every secret — review before sharing still matters); full\n119\thistories can exceed the target's context (size is reported before launch);\n120\tcrashes mid-turn leave partial capture, which the ledger tolerates by design.\n121\t\n122\t## Roadmap\n123\t\n124\tToward an npm release (decided 2026-07-21; deepen the two existing targets\n125\tbefore broadening):\n126\t\n127\t- Publish `conversation-ledger` to npm (name is unclaimed), then swap the\n128\t  `file:` dependency for a semver range — `prepublishOnly` refuses to publish\n129\t  until this happens. Deliberately deferred while both packages are iterated\n130\t  on and dogfooded for a few days.\n131\t- Adapter-drift automation stage 2: the daily check\n132\t  (`.github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml`) currently opens a tracking issue on\n133\t  drift; the commented-out follow-on job hands the issue to a Claude Code\n134\t  action that revalidates the spec against the new CLI release and drafts the\n135\t  PR. Needs an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` repo secret and comfort with CI pushing\n136\t  branches.\n137\t- Revalidation tooling exists and is the bar for widening version pins:\n138\t  `npm run smoke:interactive` (real-TUI render check, both targets) plus\n139\t  `scripts/probe-codex-content.mjs` (headless model-recall probe).\n140\t- Still-open verification gaps from the spec docs: large/long histories\n141\t  (size cliffs, Codex auto-compaction), timestamp-format tolerance,\n142\t  sessionId/filename mismatch, duplicate or dangling uuid handling.\n143\t- **Encrypted-reasoning replay** *(shipped, needs a turnbridge version bump)*\n144\t  — Codex's `reasoning` items are ciphertext only OpenAI's servers can\n145\t  decrypt; conversation-ledger 0.10.0 preserves them losslessly and opaquely\n146\t  (`kind: \"reasoning\"`, ciphertext in `raw.data`, `content` a bare opacity\n147\t  marker). `listConversations` (`src/conversations.ts`) now fetches\n148\t  `reasoning` events alongside `conversation_turn`s — `readEvents`'s `kind`\n149\t  filter is exact-match only, so it fetches unfiltered and narrows\n150\t  client-side — and carries them through `ConversationSummary.events` in\n151\t  seq order; `turnCount` still counts only visible turns.\n152\t  `src/targets/codex.ts`'s `buildRolloutLines` replays each reasoning\n153\t  event's verbatim `raw.data` response_item line at its correct seq position\n154\t  when `event.producer.source === \"codex\"` — gated per-event, not\n155\t  per-conversation, even though today's data model (a `ConversationSummary`\n156\t  groups by one native session id, hence one source) makes that equivalent\n157\t  to a per-conversation check in practice; genuine multi-hop carry-over\n158\t  (reconstructing an ancestor hop's reasoning via the lineage chain when\n159\t  re-bridging) is deliberately not built and stays a follow-up. Never\n160\t  applies to a Claude Code target: foreign reasoning can't be forged as a\n161\t  native reasoning item, so the only real switch is whether provider-matched\n162\t  replay happens, not what it's coerced into — unreadable/foreign reasoning\n163\t  is still folded into labeled text as before. On by default (decided\n164\t  2026-07-23); opt out with `--no-reasoning-replay` or\n165\t  `{\"reasoningReplay\": false}` in `~/.turnbridge/config.json` (`src/config.ts`).\n166\t  No ownership gate — replay applies to any synced conversation, not just\n167\t  the current user's own, per 2026-07-23 decision. The fabricated session's\n168\t  import notice (`buildRolloutLines`) is conditional: it discloses the\n169\t  replayed-block count when replay happened instead of the blanket \"hidden\n170\t  reasoning ... not transferred\" claim, and still states that claim for\n171\t  everything else in the same session. Empirically verified vi