{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Your questions have been answered: \"Architecture fact: a ConversationSummary is always single-source today — it's grouped by one native conversation.id, which belongs to exactly one adapter (codex or claude-code). So a codex→claude→codex chain doesn't produce one summary with mixed producer.source events; hop B (the claude-fabricated session, once really used) is captured as its own all-claude-code conversation, and hop A's original codex reasoning ciphertext never enters it (A's turns were folded to plain text when B was fabricated). Genuine 'carry a 2-hops-back Codex leg's reasoning into a fresh fabrication' requires new code that walks the lineage chain (lineage.parentOf) back to ancestor hops and pulls in their original ledger events. Given that, what should this pass do?\"=\"Per-event gating only, no chain-walk (Recommended)\", \"Given replay is on by default with no gate the user has to opt into, should there be an escape hatch to turn it off?\"=\"Yes, add an opt-out (Recommended)\". You can now continue with these answers in mind.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sv8kokGhyRbNwXRrfhpMf3","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"8e94c8a4de8074d5913d19180e2844cbac51d55933bbb375da42b337fd81df6d","head":"a61d7e48f18594b62ae378267837151b1827b246","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:43ec7768-b4ea-485b-b6e2-ed60c3ad4a01","seq":149},"id":"ev1-ccf549c221e125c6bf039ef2af19d3686375ae4ce56fe782d8c9c5852f844eb1","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-24T06:39:04.017Z","producer":{"session_id":"43ec7768-b4ea-485b-b6e2-ed60c3ad4a01","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.10.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":