ever enters it (A's turns were folded to plain text when B was fabricated). Genuine 'carry a 2-hops-back Codex leg's reasoning into a fresh fabrication' requires new code that walks the lineage chain (lineage.parentOf) back to ancestor hops and pulls in their original ledger events. Given that, what should this pass do?":"Per-event gating only, no chain-walk (Recommended)","Given replay is on by default with no gate the user has to opt into, should there be an escape hatch to turn it off?":"Yes, add an opt-out (Recommended)"},"questions":[{"header":"Lineage depth","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"Gate replay on each event's own producer.source (not a blanket per-conversation check) so the logic is correct and forward-compatible. But don't build lineage-chain traversal now — today's data model means this is equivalent to the simple codex→codex case in practice. True cross-hop carry-over (reconstructing an ancestor hop's reasoning during re-bridging) becomes a follow-up roadmap item.","label":"Per-event gating only, no chain-walk (Recommended)"},{"description":"When re-bridging a conversation that has ancestors (lineage.parentOf), walk back through the chain, pull each ancestor's own original ledger events (not the folded-text copy), and splice in reasoning from every Codex-origin leg — real multi-hop support, materially more code and more surface for bugs.","label":"Build lineage chain-walk now"}],"question":"Architecture fact: a ConversationSummary is always single-source today — it's grouped by one native conversation.id, which belongs to exactly one adapter (codex or claude-code). So a codex→claude→codex chain doesn't produce one summary with mixed producer.source events; hop B (the claude-fabricated session, once really used) is captured as its own all-claude-code conversation, and hop A's original codex reasoning ciphertext never enters it (A's turns were folded to plain text when B was fabricated). Genuine 'carry a 2-hops-back Codex leg's reasoning into a fresh fabrication' requires new code that walks the lineage chain (lineage.parentOf) back to ancestor hops and pulls in their original ledger events. Given that, what should this pass do?"},{"header":"Escape hatch","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"A config flag (e.g. `{\"reasoning\": {\"replay\": false}}`) and/or a `--no-reasoning-replay` CLI flag. Cheap to add, gives users a lever given the still-open blob-TTL/org-auth unknowns noted in conversation-ledger's roadmap.","label":"Yes, add an opt-out (Recommended)"},{"description":"No off-switch — replay always happens when source/target match. Simplest surface; revisit if it causes problems.","label":"No, keep it unconditional for v1"}],"question":"Given replay is on by default with no gate the user has to opt into, should there be an escape hatch to turn it off?"}]},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"a517d27f-563e-4bbb-9710-a38ba591b8d0","version":"2.1.218"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-24T06:46:38.408Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
